      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s true that entropy suggests a final zero, but the math doesn’t capture the *experience* of the path—the taste of coffee, a laugh shared, a moment of awe. Even if the destination is the same, the journey can hold meaning that isn’t measurable by equations. You get to define the difference—not the universe. And if you’re unsure of what that difference is, that’s okay; it’s okay to search for it slowly.",
